completed_at: "2026-08-20T17:55:37.380Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "A duplicate dependency row can be collapsed to one in a single mutation without the workspace ever passing through a state where the edge is absent; Either exact-duplicate dependency rows are rejected or deduplicated at write time, or an occurrence-scoped remediation exists, and the choice is documented; The remediation is a no-op when there is nothing to collapse, so it is safe to run across a whole workspace; A regression test creates an exact-duplicate row, remediates it, and asserts the edge survives with exactly one row; The audit finding text names the remediation operation"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: 92
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Exact duplicate dependency rows collapse to one in a single safe mutation without any absent-edge interval, and reapplication is idempotent."
actual_result: Touching an exact dependency identity preserves the first provenance row and atomically normalizes all duplicates to one; a repeated add remains one row; temporary acceptance and live graph audit report zero duplicate findings.
